lems that not just Americans face but all humans. Overfishing, depleting entire ecosystems, no fishing regulations or quotas, public demand for fish on the dinner table, and polluting fish farms are just a few of the topics he discusses. He has written articles for The New York Times Magazine, Book Review, and in the October 2010 issue of National Geographic, he wrote an article that is a base summary of this book.","publicationYear":2010,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Cultural control","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-four-fish-the-future-of-the-last-wild-food-paul-greenberg"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Fish culture","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-four-fish-the-future-of-the-last-wild-food-paul-greenberg"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Fishery management","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-four-fish-the-future-of-the-last-wild-food-paul-greenberg"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Sea basses","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-four-fish-the-future-of-the-last-wild-food-paul-greenberg"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Tuna","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-four-fish-the-future-of-the-last-wild-food-paul-greenberg"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Codfish","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-four-fish-the-future-of-the-last-wild-food-paul-greenberg"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Salmon","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-four-fish-the-future-of-the-last-wild-food-paul-greenberg"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Hatchery vs. wild stocks","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-four-fish-the-future-of-the-last-wild-food-paul-greenberg"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Fishery resources","sourceId"